;Way to Karhad from Dam Top in Shartans-room 732
NUMBER 3646
NAME Teeth of Shartan, Steep Trail
MOUNTAIN
CALL 33
MONSTER_GROUP 55
DAY_LIGHT
*DESCRIPTION_START
A small winding trail works its way steadily upwards in the steepness of 
the mountain range. The air grows still, and begins to chill as you near 
the snowline. Along the northern side of the trail, the trees begin to 
thin a bit. Far to the south, you can barely make out a dam and the stream
near it.
*DESCRIPTION_END
ITEM 0 76 ADJ1=510 ADJ2=407 VAL2=732
EXIT N 3647
;
NUMBER 3647
NAME Shartan Trail
CALL 33
CALL 49
MOUNTAIN
DAY_LIGHT
REGION 43
CHANNEL 43
*DESCRIPTION_START
This portion of the trail leads upwards into the very edge of the line 
of snow. A few trees are laden with it. In several places, footprints
are visible in the drifted snow. To the south, most of the unquart has
disappeared, to be replaced by sturdier evergreens. Above, the sky is
clearly seen as the trail disappears over a large section of rock. 
Visible for miles is the skyline of the rocky Shartan's, stretching 
outwards, and reminding you how very far from Fayd you are.
*DESCRIPTION_END
EXIT S 3646
EXIT N 3648
;
NUMBER 3648
NAME Shartan Vista
CALL 33
CALL 49
MOUNTAIN
REGION 43
CHANNEL 43
DAY_LIGHT
*DESCRIPTION_START
The crest of this mountain is breathtaking. All around the nearby peaks 
are visible. Down below, your eyes can see clearly back to the dam, and 
on the other side of the peak, you see a small village thriving under 
the protective overhang of the mountain. Small swirls of smoke drift  
upwards, and even from the distance, you can hear the sound of dogs 
barking. Across the tiny bowl, you see on the far side a beautiful 
castle perched on the mountain. Another forest leads up and over
the far mountain. A small trail leads down into the village itself.
*DESCRIPTION_END
EXIT S 3647
ITEM 0 76 ADJ1=427 VAL2=3649
EXTEND 0 leading down to the village
;
NUMBER 3649
NAME Karhad Village Entrance
CALL 33
CALL 49
REGION 43
CHANNEL 43
FOREST
DAY_LIGHT
*DESCRIPTION_START
Before you is a wonderful sight caressing your senses. A large overhang
droops over parts of the village to the south, shielding it from the worst
of the weather. A large sleepy forest stands to the north, guarding the
village from prying eyes. A long winding dirt road circles around inside
the village. In the snow, you can see many pawprints of the sled dogs.
Directly ahead, lies a small gatehouse. Its lone sentry stands at attention.
A long windy trail leads up from the valley, and over the nearby mountainside.
*DESCRIPTION_END
