*DESCRIPTION_START
This tiny courtyard is a haven for snow. It drifts into the corners and 
along the walls in an effort to escape, until you look closer. Then, 
lines and forms begin to emerge from out of the seeming randomness. Ice 
sculptures of dogs and sleds race along tracks of drifted snow. Drivers, 
their faces masks of pure concentration work long strings of howling 
huskies, their heads shrouded in fogs of condesation. Everywhere around 
you is the beauty of this cold realm. The castle itself sits here, its 
stone walls covered heavily in ice. A large double door leads inside.
*DESCRIPTION_END
